// Detonated at a chosen point up to 37 m away, same deviation as
// assets/common/abilities/spells/evocation/acid_splash.ron (Wave 1):
// CharacterAbility::Explosion always detonates centered on the caster's own
// position (common/src/states/explosion.rs has no target-point field at
// all), which contradicts this spell's own ranged-and-relocatable beam, so
// it uses GroundAoe instead, the engine's real "detonate at a chosen point
// within range" primitive.
//
// GroundAoe also hardcodes DamageKind::Energy in
// common/src/states/ground_aoe.rs (no RON-configurable damage_kind field
// exists on this variant) -- so despite the Radiant flavor text, this deals
// generic Energy damage under the hood, same drift already documented on
// acid_splash.ron.
//
// The sheet's own "lingers ... each round ... caster can shift the beam to
// a new spot" persistence is dropped, not approximated: GroundAoe is a
// single detonation with no repeat-tick or move-the-zone mechanism. The
// compendium entry below lists duration: Instant rather than
// Concentration(60) for the same reason divine_favor.ron (Wave 1) does -- a
// 60 s "active zone" claim in the spellbook tooltip would promise a
// persistence this ability doesn't have.
GroundAoe(
    energy_cost: 60.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.6,
    delay: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    max_range: 37.0,
    radius: 3.0,
    min_falloff: 0.3,
    damage: 26,
    poise: 10,
    knockback: (strength: 0, direction: Away),
    dodgeable: Roll,
    rooted_cast: false,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Divine), cooldown: Some(12.0)),
)
